  "note": "The rebuilt Hàm Rồng bridge crosses the Mã River in two gray steel through-truss spans. A single track runs inside the braced trusses, with separate cantilevered roadways, slender steel guardrails, and one central concrete river pier. The viewer uses a fixed sea-level datum and a shallow crest in the authored deck. Short retaining approaches carry the rail deck to the sampled banks. The two roadways meet terrain-resolved approaches at separate staggered landings. The riverbed and opposite bridge remain native. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
